  "body": "Bumps [github.com/mattn/go-colorable](https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable) from 0.1.15 to 0.1.16.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable/releases\">github.com/mattn/go-colorable's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.1.16</h2>\n<h2>Improvements</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reduce parsing overhead and allocations for Windows consoles without VT support by processing text and escape sequences directly from input slices.</li>\n<li>Avoid redundant console queries and attribute resets, and reduce Windows API argument allocations.</li>\n<li>Precompute the 256-color mapping, removing first-use conversion work and concurrent initialization races.</li>\n<li>Speed up ANSI sequence stripping in <code>NonColorable</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Add regression coverage for fragmented sequences, Unicode titles, palette conversion, and real Windows console operations. CI passes on Windows, macOS, and Linux with Go 1.24, 1.25, and 1.26.</p>\n<p>Implemented in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/mattn/go-colorable/issues/84\">#84</a>. Real console output remains limited by console I/O: local benchmarks showed about 29% higher throughput for 4 KiB text with an escape sequence and about 3% for colored log lines; parser-only gains are substantially larger.</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable/compare/v0.1.15...v0.1.16\">https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable/compare/v0.1.15...v0.1.16</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable/commit/56c5db567780daeef4a4ffbb2c14d7d4b6b94b9b\"><code>56c5db5</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/mattn/go-colorable/issues/84\">#84</a> from mattn/opt-windows-combined</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable/commit/484428334f386e8f5a228c8bea07e399d5f1d61e\"><code>4844283</code></a> Integrate independently validated Windows performance improvements</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/mattn/go-colorable/compare/v0.1.15...v0.1.16\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=github.com/mattn/go-colorable&package-manager=go_modules&previous-version=0.1.15&new-version=0.1.16)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>",
